@lang en
IMPORT `law36-vn28-decisions`

-- Constructors for the fact patterns the tests and findings modules use. No rules and no
-- assertions: every figure a test turns on is passed in by the test itself, next to the
-- source line it comes from. Fields a constructor fixes (the number of wheels of an
-- automobile, its motor) are ones no test here turns on, and each says so.
-- It sits at the end of the import chain so that the tests can import it alone.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Towed vehicles`

GIVEN g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A towed vehicle`
`a trailer of gross mass in kg` g MEANS
    `A towed vehicle` WITH
        `gross design mass in kg` IS g
        `a semi-trailer`          IS FALSE

GIVEN g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A towed vehicle`
`a semi-trailer of gross mass in kg` g MEANS
    `A towed vehicle` WITH
        `gross design mass in kg` IS g
        `a semi-trailer`          IS TRUE

§§ `The general constructor`

-- Every field of `A road vehicle`, in the order the record declares them.
GIVEN nw  IS A NUMBER
      mp  IS A `A source of motive power`
      spd IS A NUMBER
      km  IS A NUMBER
      gm  IS A NUMBER
      pl  IS A NUMBER
      bf  IS A `A purpose of construction`
      st  IS A NUMBER
      sx  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      rw  IS A NUMBER
      oc  IS A BOOLEAN
      tu  IS A BOOLEAN
      sl  IS A BOOLEAN
      ar  IS A BOOLEAN
      at  IS A BOOLEAN
      dis IS A BOOLEAN
      rs  IS A BOOLEAN
      sm  IS A MAYBE `A kind of special-use machine`
      tw  IS A MAYBE `A towed vehicle`
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`the vehicle` nw mp spd km gm pl bf st sx rw oc tu sl ar at dis rs sm tw MEANS
    `A road vehicle` WITH
        `wheels`                                                    IS nw
        `motive power`                                              IS mp
        `design speed in km/h`                                      IS spd
        `kerb mass in kg`                                           IS km
        `gross design mass in kg`                                   IS gm
        `payload in kg`                                             IS pl
        `built for`                                                 IS bf
        `seats, not counting the driver's`                          IS st
        `seats of the same type of automobile with the most seats` IS sx
        `rows of seats`                                             IS rw
        `engine and cargo body on one chassis`                      IS oc
        `a semi-trailer tractor unit`                               IS tu
        `a sleeper coach`                                           IS sl
        `an articulated coach`                                      IS ar
        `automatic transmission`                                    IS at
        `a three-wheeled motorcycle for disabled persons`           IS dis
        `a significant part of its gross mass rests on the towing vehicle` IS rs
        `special-use machine kind`                                  IS sm
        `towing`                                                    IS tw

§§ `Two- and three-wheelers`

-- A petrol two- or three-wheeler carrying one passenger; gross mass and payload are not
-- turned on by any test of a two- or three-wheeler.
GIVEN n  IS A NUMBER
      cc IS A NUMBER
      s  IS A NUMBER
      k  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a petrol vehicle on` n `wheels, of` cc `cm3, designed for` s `km/h, kerb mass` k MEANS
    `the vehicle` n (`a heat engine` cc) s k (k PLUS 150) 150 `carrying persons` 1 NOTHING 1
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN n  IS A NUMBER
      kw IS A NUMBER
      s  IS A NUMBER
      k  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`an electric vehicle on` n `wheels, of` kw `kW, designed for` s `km/h, kerb mass` k MEANS
    `the vehicle` n (`an electric motor` kw) s k (k PLUS 150) 150 `carrying persons` 1 NOTHING 1
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

-- Article 57(2): a three-wheeled motorcycle built for a disabled person.
GIVEN cc IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a three-wheeled motorcycle for disabled persons, in cm3` cc MEANS
    `the vehicle` 3 (`a heat engine` cc) 60 200 350 150 `carrying persons` 1 NOTHING 1
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

§§ `Automobiles`

-- A four-wheeled automobile with a 2,000 cm3 engine designed for 100 km/h; its kerb mass is
-- the gross mass less the payload. Every test of an automobile turns on the arguments.
GIVEN bf IS A `A purpose of construction`
      st IS A NUMBER
      gm IS A NUMBER
      pl IS A NUMBER
      tw IS A MAYBE `A towed vehicle`
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`an automobile for` bf `with` st `seats,` gm `kg gross,` pl `kg payload, towing` tw MEANS
    `the vehicle` 4 (`a heat engine` 2000) 100 (gm MINUS pl) gm pl bf st NOTHING 2
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING tw

GIVEN bf IS A `A purpose of construction`
      st IS A NUMBER
      gm IS A NUMBER
      pl IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`an automatic automobile for` bf `with` st `seats,` gm `kg gross,` pl `kg payload` MEANS
    `the vehicle` 4 (`a heat engine` 2000) 100 (gm MINUS pl) gm pl bf st NOTHING 2
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

-- Article 57(4): a passenger automobile with fewer seats than the largest of its type.
GIVEN st IS A NUMBER
      sx IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a passenger automobile with` st `seats, of a type whose largest has` sx `seats` MEANS
    `the vehicle` 4 (`a heat engine` 2000) 100 3000 4000 1000 `carrying persons` st (JUST sx) 2
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN st IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a sleeper coach, berths` st MEANS
    `the vehicle` 4 (`a heat engine` 9000) 100 12000 16000 4000 `carrying persons` st NOTHING 2
                  FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN st IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`an articulated coach, seats` st MEANS
    `the vehicle` 6 (`a heat engine` 9000) 80 16000 24000 8000 `carrying persons` st NOTHING 2
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN gm IS A NUMBER
      tw IS A MAYBE `A towed vehicle`
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a semi-trailer tractor unit of` gm `kg gross, towing` tw MEANS
    `the vehicle` 6 (`a heat engine` 11000) 90 (gm MINUS 1000) gm 1000 `carrying goods` 1 NOTHING 1
                  FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING tw

-- A four-wheeled motorised vehicle of Article 34(1)(d)-(đ), every limb a parameter.
GIVEN bf IS A `A purpose of construction`
      st IS A NUMBER
      s  IS A NUMBER
      k  IS A NUMBER
      oc IS A BOOLEAN
      rw IS A NUMBER
      mp IS A `A source of motive power`
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a four-wheeler for` bf `with` st `seats, designed for` s `km/h, kerb mass` k `, one chassis` oc `, rows of seats` rw `, motor` mp MEANS
    `the vehicle` 4 mp s k (k PLUS 500) 500 bf st NOTHING rw
                  oc FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

§§ `Special-use machines, trailers and rudimentary vehicles`

GIVEN pl IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a tractor with payload in kg` pl MEANS
    `the vehicle` 4 (`a heat engine` 3000) 30 2500 (2500 PLUS pl) pl `carrying goods` 1 NOTHING 1
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST `a tractor`) NOTHING

GIVEN g  IS A NUMBER
      rs IS A BOOLEAN
      sm IS A MAYBE `A kind of special-use machine`
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a towed vehicle of` g `kg gross, resting partly on the towing vehicle` rs `, special-use kind` sm MEANS
    `the vehicle` 2 `none: the vehicle is towed` 0 1000 g (g MINUS 1000) `carrying goods` 0 NOTHING 0
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE rs sm NOTHING

GIVEN mp IS A `A source of motive power`
GIVETH A `A road vehicle`
`a bicycle moved by` mp MEANS
    `the vehicle` 2 mp 25 25 125 100 `carrying persons` 1 NOTHING 1
                  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING

§§ `Licences and drivers`

GIVEN c   IS A `A licence class`
      i   IS A DATE
      e   IS A MAYBE DATE
      r   IS A `A restriction on a licence`
      pts IS A NUMBER
      rv  IS A MAYBE DATE
      wd  IS A MAYBE `A period`
GIVETH A `A driving licence`
`a Vietnamese licence of` c `issued on` i `, printed expiry` e `, restriction` r `, points` pts `, revoked on` rv `, withdrawn` wd MEANS
    `A driving licence` WITH
        `class`                          IS c
        `issued by`                      IS `a competent Vietnamese authority`
        `date of issue`                  IS i
        `expiry date printed on it`      IS e
        `restriction`                    IS r
        `points remaining`               IS pts
        `revoked under Article 62(5) on` IS rv
        `right to use withdrawn`         IS wd

-- An Article 57 licence with no printed expiry, no restriction, 12 points, never revoked.
GIVEN c IS A `A licence class under Article 57`
      i IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A driving licence`
`a licence of` c `issued on` i MEANS
    `a Vietnamese licence of` (`a class under Article 57` c) `issued on` i `, printed expiry` NOTHING `, restriction` `no restriction` `, points` 12 `, revoked on` NOTHING `, withdrawn` NOTHING

GIVEN f IS A `A licence class issued before 1 January 2025`
      i IS A DATE
      e IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `A driving licence`
`a licence of` f `issued on` i `, expiring` e MEANS
    `a Vietnamese licence of` (`a class issued before this Law` f) `issued on` i `, printed expiry` e `, restriction` `no restriction` `, points` 12 `, revoked on` NOTHING `, withdrawn` NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `A licence class`
GIVETH A `A driving licence`
`a foreign licence of` c MEANS
    `A driving licence` WITH
        `class`                          IS c
        `issued by`                      IS `a foreign or international issuer`
        `date of issue`                  IS YMD 2025 6 1
        `expiry date printed on it`      IS NOTHING
        `restriction`                    IS `no restriction`
        `points remaining`               IS 12
        `revoked under Article 62(5) on` IS NOTHING
        `right to use withdrawn`         IS NOTHING

GIVEN b  IS A DATE
      s  IS A `A sex`
      ls IS A LIST OF `A driving licence`
      mc IS A BOOLEAN
      lc IS A BOOLEAN
      ar IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A driver`
`a driver born on` b `, of sex` s `, holding` ls `, machine certificate` mc `, law certificate` lc `, army or police on duty` ar MEANS
    `A driver` WITH
        `date of birth`                                           IS b
        `sex`                                                     IS s
        `driving licences`                                        IS ls
        `holds a certificate to operate this special-use machine` IS mc
        `holds a certificate of training in road-traffic law`     IS lc
        `in the army or police, on defence or security duty`      IS ar
        `a learner or examinee in a training or test automobile on its route, with an instructor or examiner` IS FALSE

GIVEN b  IS A DATE
      s  IS A `A sex`
      ls IS A LIST OF `A driving licence`
GIVETH A `A driver`
`a civilian born on` b `, of sex` s `, holding` ls MEANS
    `a driver born on` b `, of sex` s `, holding` ls `, machine certificate` FALSE `, law certificate` FALSE `, army or police on duty` FALSE

§§ `Tests of the driver`

GIVEN m  IS A `A medium tested`
      x  IS A NUMBER
      en IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      dr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A test of the driver`
`a test of` m `finding` x `, endogenous` en `, prohibited drug` dr MEANS
    `A test of the driver` WITH
        `medium`                                                   IS m
        `alcohol concentration found`                              IS x
        `found endogenous by the Ministry of Health's method`      IS en
        `a narcotic or another stimulant the law prohibits was found` IS dr

§§ `Registrations and registered vehicles`

GIVEN rc IS A MAYBE DATE
      rp IS A MAYBE DATE
      tr IS A BOOLEAN
      au IS A BOOLEAN
      dm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A registration`
`a registration with certificate revoked` rc `, plate revoked` rp `, ownership transferred` tr `, auction plate` au `, damaged beyond use` dm MEANS
    `A registration` WITH
        `registration certificate revoked on`                       IS rc
        `plate revoked on`                                          IS rp
        `ownership transferred`                                     IS tr
        `the plate was won at auction`                              IS au
        `a duty-free or temporarily imported vehicle of a foreign body re-exported, transferred or destroyed` IS FALSE
        `registration term in a special economic or border-gate zone expired` IS FALSE
        `records forged, or chassis or engine number changed unlawfully` IS FALSE
        `engine removed to register another vehicle`                IS FALSE
        `damaged beyond use`                                        IS dm
        `scrapped, or lost and not found, and the owner asked for revocation` IS FALSE
        `registered or plated contrary to law`                      IS FALSE

`a registration with nothing recorded` MEANS
    `a registration with certificate revoked` NOTHING `, plate revoked` NOTHING `, ownership transferred` FALSE `, auction plate` FALSE `, damaged beyond use` FALSE

GIVEN v  IS A `A road vehicle`
      y  IS A NUMBER
      e  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      b  IS A MAYBE `A road vehicle`
      eb IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      mil IS A BOOLEAN
      r  IS A `A registration`
GIVETH A `A registered vehicle`
`registered` v `, made in` y `, life ending` e `, before conversion` b `, ending` eb `, military` mil `, with` r MEANS
    `A registered vehicle` WITH
        `vehicle`                                                     IS v
        `year of manufacture`                                         IS y
        `the year its service life ends under the Government's rules for its present kind` IS e
        `before conversion`                                           IS b
        `the year its service life ends under the Government's rules for its kind before conversion` IS eb
        `a military or police vehicle for defence or security`        IS mil
        `registration`                                                IS r
        `registration certificate issued and plate fitted`           IS TRUE
        `technical safety and environmental protection assured, as certified on the day asked about` IS TRUE

GIVEN v IS A `A road vehicle`
      y IS A NUMBER
      e IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      r IS A `A registration`
GIVETH A `A registered vehicle`
`the civilian vehicle` v `, made in` y `, life ending` e `, with` r MEANS
    `registered` v `, made in` y `, life ending` e `, before conversion` NOTHING `, ending` NOTHING `, military` FALSE `, with` r

-- Article 56(5): a learner in a training automobile on a training route, with an instructor.
GIVEN b IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A driver`
`a learner born on` b MEANS
    `A driver` WITH
        `date of birth`                                           IS b
        `sex`                                                     IS `female`
        `driving licences`                                        IS EMPTY
        `holds a certificate to operate this special-use machine` IS FALSE
        `holds a certificate of training in road-traffic law`     IS FALSE
        `in the army or police, on defence or security duty`      IS FALSE
        `a learner or examinee in a training or test automobile on its route, with an instructor or examiner` IS TRUE

-- A vehicle made in 2020, with no service life supplied, its Article 35(1) papers as given.
GIVEN v  IS A `A road vehicle`
      r  IS A `A registration`
      pl IS A BOOLEAN
      ok IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A registered vehicle`
`the papers of` v `, with` r `, registered and plated` pl `, inspected` ok MEANS
    `A registered vehicle` WITH
        `vehicle`                                                     IS v
        `year of manufacture`                                         IS 2020
        `the year its service life ends under the Government's rules for its present kind` IS NOTHING
        `before conversion`                                           IS NOTHING
        `the year its service life ends under the Government's rules for its kind before conversion` IS NOTHING
        `a military or police vehicle for defence or security`        IS FALSE
        `registration`                                                IS r
        `registration certificate issued and plate fitted`           IS pl
        `technical safety and environmental protection assured, as certified on the day asked about` IS ok

§§ `Events on the road`

GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
      u IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An event on the road`
`an event: collision` c `, in road traffic` i `, unintended` u `, harm` h MEANS
    `An event on the road` WITH
        `a collision`                                                       IS c
        `involving people or vehicles participating in road traffic`        IS i
        `against the will of those participating in road traffic`           IS u
        `harm to the life, health or property of a person, or to the property of a body` IS h
